;; db: bench_hub
;; THE PATHOLOGICAL CASE.  R = spokes->hub, S = hub->spokes, so R join S
;; enumerates n^2 (a,hub,c) triples; T's values are disjoint from R and S,
;; so nothing ever joins.  T carries a weight column: the extra free
;; variable keeps it from ever being scheduled as the driver, so the
;; explosive middle join is unavoidable without filters.  A semijoin filter
;; on T right after the driver (is the driver's spoke among T's endpoints?)
;; prunes every driver tuple: O(n^2) collapses to O(n).
table (redge int int)
table (sedge int int)
table (tedge int int int)
table (tri int int int)

rule (redge A B) (sedge B C) (tedge C A W) --> (tri A B C)
